Programs made with Qt Widgets can paint their windows on the graphics card the desktop gives them (ORDER 518 and 554; Daniel, 2026-11-11: "why can't we enhance qwidget to respect our gpu choice?"). QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT=batch records a window's painting and draws it in a few draw calls through the window's RHI, with the raster engine's picture; QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT=opengl paints through Qt's OpenGL paint engine. Painting on the processor stays the default, and the three ways stay the person's choice on the Graphics page (o518-0001 to o518-0014, o518-0021, o518-0022, o554-0001).

A program asked to paint on the graphics card that cannot start that painting says so through QT_WIDGETS_GPU_PAINT_TELL and paints on the processor, and a way a desktop chose for a program is that program's alone (o518-0015, o518-0018).

Element depth on the graphics card moves each item by its exact share, parts of a pixel included; where the EGL has no surface with two views (NVIDIA's own) the pair is one buffer twice as wide, declared full side by side (o518-0017).

The frame Qt draws around a window is placed and sized as its buffers are rounded at a fractional scale (o518-0016; QTBUG-149635 is related and open).

At a fractional scale the pair on the graphics card is two eyes of one whole width in device pixels, each painted from its own left edge and placed whole pixels apart (o554-0002). Before, twice the rounded width of one view was not the rounded width of two, so the window was shown flat at every width that is not whole at that scale. A window whose frame Qt draws itself gets the pair too (o554-0003, o554-0004).

The processor-painted pair has the same form at a fractional scale: a buffer of two eyes of one whole width, each eye painted into its own half; its shifts stay whole pixels of the window (o554-0005). Before, at 125 % every item of such a window sat up to 0.7 device pixels off its parallax.

zink asked for by name without Mesa's own presentation path (LIBGL_KOPPER_DISABLE) presents one view where it lists two; the pair then goes side by side into one buffer instead of being shown at half width (o554-0006). The edition's NVIDIA session sets that variable, and nothing changes there.
